estingly, megabats—like fruit bats—have huge, prominent eyes and don't use echolocation at all!) So, your grandma was using a perfectly good, time-honored figure of speech! It just happens to be based on thousands of years of human observation before we had the technology to understand exactly what bats were actually doing.
